Refinitiv Treasury OMM Application
Overview
This Spring Boot application consumes real-time U.S. Treasury market data (e.g., US2YT=RR) from Refinitiv’s Elektron Message API (EMA) using the chain RIC 0#USTSY=. It processes bid/ask prices and yields, stores them in an Oracle database, and uses ZooKeeper for leader election to ensure only one node processes data. The application operates Monday to Friday, 3 AM–11 PM IST, and sends email notifications for exceptions. Metrics are exposed via Micrometer and Prometheus for monitoring.
Features

Subscribes to Refinitiv chain RIC 0#USTSY= and processes constituent RICs (e.g., US2YT=RR).
Handles market price messages (BID, ASK, YLD_1, ASK_YLD) using ArrayBlockingQueue (capacity: 10,000).
Batches and upserts data to Oracle (batch size: 1000) with retry logic.
Leader election via ZooKeeper ensures single-node processing.
Sends exception emails using JavaMailSender (e.g., Gmail SMTP).
Exposes metrics (/actuator/prometheus) for queue size, subscriptions, and latency.
Runs on port 8095 with Asia/Kolkata timezone.

Prerequisites

Java: 17 or higher
Maven: 3.8.0 or higher
Oracle Database: 12c or higher with TREASURY_PRICE_T and TREASURY_PRICE_TAB types, and treasury_feeds.load_treasury_prices procedure.
ZooKeeper: 3.7.0 or higher
Refinitiv EMA: SDK for market data access
SMTP Server: Gmail or another provider for email notifications
Dependencies: Listed in pom.xml (e.g., Spring Boot, Oracle JDBC, Curator, Micrometer, JavaMail)

Setup

Clone the Repository:
git clone <repository-url>
cd refinitiv-treasury-omm


Configure Application Properties:Edit src/main/resources/application.properties:
spring.datasource.url=jdbc:oracle:thin:@localhost:1521:ORCL
spring.datasource.username=your_username
spring.datasource.password=your_password
refinitiv.host=your-refinitiv-host
refinitiv.port=14002
spring.mail.host=smtp.gmail.com
spring.mail.port=587
spring.mail.username=your-email@gmail.com
spring.mail.password=your-app-specific-password
app.error.email.to=recipient@example.com
zookeeper.connect-string=localhost:2181


Generate a Gmail app-specific password: Google Account > Security > 2-Step Verification > App passwords.
Ensure EmaConfig.xml is in src/main/resources with correct host/port placeholders.


Set Up Oracle Database:Execute oracle_types_and_procedure.sql to create types and stored procedure:
CREATE OR REPLACE TYPE TREASURY_PRICE_T AS OBJECT (
    ric VARCHAR2(50),
    timestamp TIMESTAMP,
    bid_yield NUMBER,
    ask_yield NUMBER,
    bid_price NUMBER,
    ask_price NUMBER,
    update_type VARCHAR2(20),
    last_update TIMESTAMP
);
/
CREATE OR REPLACE TYPE TREASURY_PRICE_TAB AS TABLE OF TREASURY_PRICE_T;
/
CREATE OR REPLACE PACKAGE treasury_feeds AS
    PROCEDURE load_treasury_prices(p_prices IN TREASURY_PRICE_TAB);
END treasury_feeds;
/
CREATE OR REPLACE PACKAGE BODY treasury_feeds AS
    PROCEDURE load_treasury_prices(p_prices IN TREASURY_PRICE_TAB) IS
    BEGIN
        FORALL i IN 1..p_prices.COUNT
            INSERT INTO Treasury_data (ric, timestamp, bid_yield, ask_yield, bid_price, ask_price, update_type, last_update)
            VALUES (
                p_prices(i).ric,
                p_prices(i).timestamp,
                p_prices(i).bid_yield,
                p_prices(i).ask_yield,
                p_prices(i).bid_price,
                p_prices(i).ask_price,
                p_prices(i).update_type,
                p_prices(i).last_update
            );
        COMMIT;
    EXCEPTION
        WHEN OTHERS THEN
            ROLLBACK;
            RAISE;
    END load_treasury_prices;
END treasury_feeds;
/


Start ZooKeeper:
zkServer.sh start


Install Dependencies:
mvn clean install



Running the Application

Start the Application:
mvn spring-boot:run


The application starts on http://localhost:8095.
If the node is the leader and within operating hours (3 AM–11 PM IST, Mon–Fri), it subscribes to 0#USTSY= and processes RICs like US2YT=RR.


Manual Triggers:

Start consumer: curl -X POST http://localhost:8095/trigger-start-consumer
Process messages: curl -X POST http://localhost:8095/trigger-process-messages
Flush batch: curl -X POST http://localhost:8095/trigger-flush-batch
Check leadership: curl http://localhost:8095/leadership-status



Testing

Run Unit Tests:
mvn clean test


Tests in RefinitivTreasuryOmmApplicationTests.java cover RefinitivOmmConsumer, TreasuryDataService, LeaderElectionService, TreasuryDataRepository, and ExceptionEmailService.
Achieves 100% line/branch coverage (JaCoCo report in target/jacoco-report).


Verify US2YT=RR Processing:

Check logs for:Subscribed to chain constituent, ric=US2YT=RR, handle=..., active_subscriptions=...
Queued TreasuryPriceDto, ric=US2YT=RR, queue_size=...
Processed batch, size=..., duration_ms=...


Query Oracle:SELECT * FROM Treasury_data WHERE ric = 'US2YT=RR';





Monitoring

Actuator Endpoints:

Health: curl http://localhost:8095/actuator/health
Metrics: curl http://localhost:8095/actuator/prometheus
Key metrics:
message_queue_size: Current queue size.
consumer_subscriptions_active: Number of subscribed RICs (e.g., US2YT=RR).
queue_dropped_messages_total: Dropped messages due to full queue.
queue_offer_latency_seconds: Latency for queue offer operations.
scheduled_task_invocations_total: Task invocation counts (e.g., startConsumer, processMessages).




Logs:

Located in console or configured log file (e.g., application.log).
Set logging.level.com.example.refinitivtreasury=DEBUG for detailed logs.



Troubleshooting

No Data Processed:
Verify node is leader: curl http://localhost:8095/leadership-status.
Check operating hours (3 AM–11 PM IST, Mon–Fri).
Ensure refinitiv.host and refinitiv.port are correct in application.properties.


Email Notification Issues:
Verify SMTP settings and app-specific password.
Check logs for Failed to send exception email.


Database Errors:
Ensure Oracle types and procedure are created.
Check SQLException in logs and email reports.


ZooKeeper Issues:
Verify ZooKeeper is running: zkServer.sh status.
Check zookeeper.connect-string.



